    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600">

                <pb facs="0893" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.311F1/22: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-02T12:00:00-04:00">May 2,
                            1933—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>44. Your 106, May 1. The Department has designated Mr. Henry Morgenthau, senior,
                    to serve as its expert on the Wheat Conference on <pb facs="0894" n="792"
                        xml:id="pg792"/> May 10. If the League will convey its invitation<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d600-f1"/> to the Department the Department will transmit it.
                    Mr. Morgenthau is sailing tonight for Geneva.</p>
                <p>The Department will do its best to expedite the matter by talking with the
                    Canadian Minister and if possible also with the Argentine Delegation which has
                    just arrived in Washington.</p>
                <p>Mr. Morgenthau is accompanied by Mr. George C. Haas of the Farm Board as an
                    advisor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d600-f1" n="8" xml:id="d600-f1-content">
                <p>Substance of invitation contained in telegram No. 107, May 3, from the Consul at
                    Geneva (561.311F1/23).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
